{%- comment -%}
  ElmsNest v2 COLLECTION — 4.1 THE GATE: screen 1 (collection WINNING-SPEC 4.1).

  The only section that renders snippets/elmsnest-v2-ground-collection (3.1), and the first section in
  templates/collection.json, so it is also the page's one place to print the glyph sprite and the card
  stylesheet before anything below it draws a plate or a card (CONTRACT-COLL 4 and 6, risk 11).

  What has to fit inside 1440x900 AND 390x844, on all FIVE urls (4.1 non-negotiable 1):
    where you are      - collection.title as a real, visible h1 in Frank Ruhl Libre over a full-bleed
                         night photograph. The sr-only SEO h1 dies (AUDIT 4.3).
    what it is for     - one authored deck line and the APPROVED suits/does-not-suit pair (graft C8),
                         verbatim from BRIEF 3, per collection, never a new negative.
    how big the shop is- the counts line, every figure from Liquid: products_count, the summed variant
                         count and the price span of collection.products.
    one real lamp      - the pin: a lit dot, a hairline stem and a gold tag that names the lamp and
                         prints its REAL first-axis value, from snippets/elmsnest-v2-coll-axis.
    a price and a route- one pinned product card, elmsnest-v2-pdp-card with variant:'scene' - the scrim
                         card of 3.1, used exactly twice on the page and never hand-rolled.

  ONE template serves all five collection urls (5.1), so nothing here may be a single typed value that
  is only true on one of them. Every per-collection string is resolved from collection.handle with the
  approved copy as the default, every per-collection number comes from the collection object or from
  the axis parser, and collection_map is the one setting that carries the per-url pin and focus.

  No JS: the photograph, the h1, the deck, the suits pair, the counts line, the pin and the card are all
  server-rendered; the card's buy control is elmsnest-v2-buy, which POSTs to routes.cart_add_url for a
  single-variant product and is a plain link otherwise. Only the pin's dot-then-stem lighting needs JS,
  and without it the pin is simply drawn lit. Reduced motion: the same, with no transition.

  Do-not, enforced here: no banner band, no breadcrumb strip, no toolbar (4.1 n-n 3, 6.1); no sale UI
  (6.4); no product title in the serif (6.11); no typed number (6.19); radius 0 except the pill (6.14);
  logical properties only (3.1); no cream, beige or brown surface (6.10).

  Shopify schema note (2026-09-03, integration): a setting LABEL is capped at 70 characters and the
  whole file is rejected past it, so collection_map's field list lives in its info string.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% render 'elmsnest-v2-ground-collection' %}
{% render 'elmsnest-v2-coll-glyph', sprite: true %}
{% render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-card', css: true %}
{%- liquid
  assign env2_ready = false
  if collection != blank and collection.title != blank
    assign env2_ready = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if env2_ready -%}
{%- liquid
  assign env2_h = collection.handle | default: ''
  assign env2_all = false
  if env2_h == 'all' or env2_h == ''
    assign env2_all = true
  endif

  # the per-url row of collection_map, one line per collection:
  # handle|pin product|pin_x|pin_y|pin_x_m|pin_y_m|focus desktop|focus mobile|card image index
  # Fields after the handle are optional; an empty field falls back to the matching setting below.
  assign env2_row = ''
  assign env2_maptxt = section.settings.collection_map | default: ''
  if env2_maptxt != blank
    assign env2_maprows = env2_maptxt | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
    for env2_r in env2_maprows
      assign env2_r = env2_r | strip_html | strip
      if env2_r != ''
        assign env2_f = env2_r | split: '|'
        assign env2_k = env2_f[0] | strip
        if env2_k == env2_h
          assign env2_row = env2_r
        endif
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  assign env2_mf = env2_row | split: '|'
  assign env2_map_pin = env2_mf[1] | default: '' | strip
  assign env2_map_x = env2_mf[2] | default: '' | strip
  assign env2_map_y = env2_mf[3] | default: '' | strip
  assign env2_map_xm = env2_mf[4] | default: '' | strip
  assign env2_map_ym = env2_mf[5] | default: '' | strip
  assign env2_map_fd = env2_mf[6] | default: '' | strip
  assign env2_map_fm = env2_mf[7] | default: '' | strip
  assign env2_map_ci = env2_mf[8] | default: '' | strip
-%}
{%- liquid
  # Copy. Every default below is the approved wording of 4.1 and BRIEF 3 for that collection; a merchant
  # setting overrides it on every url at once, which is why the defaults are resolved per handle here.
  assign env2_eyebrow = section.settings.eyebrow | default: ''
  if env2_eyebrow == ''
    if env2_all
      assign env2_eyebrow = 'ערב אחד · כל החנות'
    else
      assign env2_eyebrow = 'ערב אחד בחצר · קולקציה'
    endif
  endif

  assign env2_deck = section.settings.deck | default: ''
  assign env2_suits = section.settings.suits_line | default: ''
  if env2_h == 'גרילנדות-ותאורה-דקורטיבית'
    assign env2_deck_d = 'מהשולחן, דרך העצים והערוגה, עד הגדר בסוף החצר.'
    assign env2_suits_d = 'מתאים כדי ליצור אווירה. לא מתאים אם צריך אור חזק — זו אינה מטרתה.'
  elsif env2_h == 'תאורת-שביל-סולארית'
    assign env2_deck_d = 'מהשער עד הדלת, בלי לנחש איפה המדרגה.'
    assign env2_suits_d = 'מתאים כדי לראות את הדרך. לא מתאים כשהמקום כמעט אינו מקבל אור יום.'
  elsif env2_h == 'solar-wall-lights'
    assign env2_deck_d = 'קיר אחד, וכל מה שלידו נראה אחרת.'
    assign env2_suits_d = 'מתאים כדי להאיר נקודה מסוימת. לא מתאים כשנדרש אור חזק וקבוע לאורך כל הלילה.'
  elsif env2_h == 'ספוטים-ופרוז-קטורים-סולאריים'
    assign env2_deck_d = 'אור אחד, מכוון בדיוק לאן שצריך.'
    assign env2_suits_d = 'מתאים כדי להאיר עץ או ערוגה. לא מתאים כשנדרשת התקנה מיוחדת או חיבור קבוע.'
  else
    assign env2_deck_d = 'עשרים ושבע מנורות, לפי הסדר שבו נדלק הערב.'
    assign env2_suits_d = ''
  endif
  if env2_deck == ''
    assign env2_deck = env2_deck_d
  endif
  if env2_suits == ''
    assign env2_suits = env2_suits_d
  endif

  # The h1 is collection.title and nothing else (4.1 n-n 2). 3.2 asks for a second line in --env2-glow,
  # so the last N words of the real title are moved to that line. A title with no more words than N
  # stays whole and stays ink - the glow line is never invented and never a word the shop did not write.
  assign env2_gw = section.settings.title_glow_words | default: 1 | plus: 0
  assign env2_words = collection.title | strip | split: ' '
  assign env2_wn = env2_words.size
  assign env2_t1 = collection.title | strip
  assign env2_t2 = ''
  if env2_gw > 0 and env2_wn > env2_gw
    assign env2_cut = env2_wn | minus: env2_gw
    assign env2_t1 = ''
    assign env2_t2 = ''
    for env2_w in env2_words
      if forloop.index0 < env2_cut
        assign env2_t1 = env2_t1 | append: ' ' | append: env2_w
      else
        assign env2_t2 = env2_t2 | append: ' ' | append: env2_w
      endif
    endfor
    assign env2_t1 = env2_t1 | strip
    assign env2_t2 = env2_t2 | strip
  endif
-%}
{%- liquid
  # The counts line. products_count, the summed variant count and the price span are read off the
  # collection, never typed (6.19). collection.products is capped at 50 per page by Shopify and the
  # catalogue is 27, so the sum is the whole collection; the ledger section owns pagination (3.7).
  assign env2_nv = 0
  assign env2_lo = 0
  assign env2_hi = 0
  for env2_p in collection.products
    assign env2_nv = env2_nv | plus: env2_p.variants.size
    if env2_lo == 0
      assign env2_lo = env2_p.price_min
    endif
    if env2_p.price_min < env2_lo
      assign env2_lo = env2_p.price_min
    endif
    if env2_p.price_max > env2_hi
      assign env2_hi = env2_p.price_max
    endif
  endfor
  assign env2_lo_s = env2_lo | money_without_currency
  assign env2_hi_s = env2_hi | money_without_currency
  assign env2_span = ''
  if env2_hi > 0
    assign env2_span = env2_lo_s
    if env2_hi > env2_lo
      assign env2_span = env2_lo_s | append: '–' | append: env2_hi_s
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- liquid
  # The pinned product. ONE template, five urls, so a product picker alone cannot answer; the resolution
  # order is collection_map, then the picker, then an automatic choice: the first available product that
  # is measured on its own first axis AND has a text-free photograph, then the first available product
  # with a photograph, then the first available product. The card and the pin name the same lamp.
  assign env2_pin_set = '0'
  assign env2_best = '0'
  assign env2_alt = '0'
  assign env2_any = '0'
-%}
{%- if env2_map_pin != '' and all_products[env2_map_pin] != blank -%}
  {%- assign env2_pin = all_products[env2_map_pin] -%}{%- assign env2_pin_set = '1' -%}
{%- elsif section.settings.pin_product != blank -%}
  {%- assign env2_pin = section.settings.pin_product -%}{%- assign env2_pin_set = '1' -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if env2_pin_set == '0' -%}
  {%- for env2_p in collection.products -%}
    {%- if env2_p.available -%}
      {%- if env2_any == '0' -%}{%- assign env2_c_any = env2_p -%}{%- assign env2_any = '1' -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- capture env2_nc -%}{%- render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-image', product: env2_p, emit: 'no_clean' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- assign env2_nc = env2_nc | strip -%}
      {%- if env2_nc == '0' -%}
        {%- if env2_alt == '0' -%}{%- assign env2_c_alt = env2_p -%}{%- assign env2_alt = '1' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if env2_best == '0' -%}
          {%- capture env2_a0 -%}{%- render 'elmsnest-v2-coll-axis', product: env2_p -%}{%- endcapture -%}
          {%- assign env2_m0 = env2_a0 | split: '~~R~~' | first | split: '~~F~~' -%}
          {%- if env2_m0[9] == '1' -%}{%- assign env2_c_best = env2_p -%}{%- assign env2_best = '1' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if env2_best == '1' -%}
    {%- assign env2_pin = env2_c_best -%}{%- assign env2_pin_set = '1' -%}
  {%- elsif env2_alt == '1' -%}
    {%- assign env2_pin = env2_c_alt -%}{%- assign env2_pin_set = '1' -%}
  {%- elsif env2_any == '1' -%}
    {%- assign env2_pin = env2_c_any -%}{%- assign env2_pin_set = '1' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- liquid
  # The axis model of the pinned lamp - the single source of the pin tag's value, the card's axis
  # caption and the derived per-unit line (CONTRACT-COLL 2). A snippet's assigns do not reach the
  # caller, so the model is printed and split back.
  assign env2_unit = ''
  assign env2_ulab = ''
  assign env2_min = ''
  assign env2_meas = '0'
  assign env2_axisline = ''
  assign env2_unitline = ''
  assign env2_v1 = ''
  assign env2_nstops = 0
-%}
{%- if env2_pin_set == '1' -%}
  {%- capture env2_model -%}{%- render 'elmsnest-v2-coll-axis', product: env2_pin -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign env2_recs = env2_model | split: '~~R~~' -%}
  {%- if env2_recs.size > 1 -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign m = env2_recs[0] | split: '~~F~~'
      assign env2_unit = m[3]
      assign env2_ulab = m[4]
      assign env2_min = m[11]
      assign env2_meas = m[9]
      assign env2_nstops = env2_recs.size | minus: 1

      assign s1 = env2_recs[1] | split: '~~F~~'
      assign sN = env2_recs | last | split: '~~F~~'
      assign env2_v1 = s1[2]
      if env2_v1 == 'Default Title' or env2_v1 == 'Title'
        assign env2_v1 = ''
      endif

        # the axis caption: the first value and the last, both real option values, escaped here because
        # the card prints the string it is handed.
      if env2_v1 != ''
        assign env2_axisline = env2_v1 | escape
        if env2_nstops > 1
          assign env2_vN = sN[2] | escape
          assign env2_axisline = env2_axisline | append: ' · ' | append: env2_vN
        endif
      endif

        # the derived per-unit figure at the entry price (graft C2). The parser computed it; this section
        # only prefixes the tilde, and the tilde goes INSIDE the bdi or the RTL algorithm moves it to the
        # far edge and the line reads "9.99 ILS per metre approx" backwards (CONTRACT-COLL 3.5).
      if section.settings.show_unit_price and s1[13] != ''
        assign env2_unitline = '<bdi>≈' | append: s1[13] | append: '</bdi> ' | append: s1[14]
      endif
    -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- liquid
  # the buy label of the card, derived from the axis the buyer will actually be choosing on.
  assign env2_act = section.settings.card_action_label | default: ''
  assign env2_axname = ''
  if env2_pin_set == '1'
    assign env2_axname = env2_pin.options_with_values[0].name | default: ''
  endif
  if env2_act == ''
    if env2_unit == 'm'
      assign env2_act = 'לבחירת אורך'
    elsif env2_unit == 'qty'
      assign env2_act = 'לבחירת כמות'
    elsif env2_unit == 'area'
      assign env2_act = 'לבחירת גודל'
    elsif env2_axname contains 'צבע'
      assign env2_act = 'לבחירת גוון'
    elsif env2_axname contains 'גוון'
      assign env2_act = 'לבחירת גוון'
    else
      assign env2_act = 'לבחירת דגם'
    endif
  endif

  # the pin tag: the lamp, then its real value. A measured axis prints the smallest length or quantity
  # it is sold in; an unmeasured one prints its first real option value when that value is short enough
  # to be a tag; otherwise the house price rule. 4.1 n-n 4 - real data or no pin.
  assign env2_pinname = section.settings.pin_label | default: ''
  if env2_pinname == '' and env2_pin_set == '1'
    assign env2_pintitle = env2_pin.title | default: ''
    assign env2_pinname = env2_pintitle | split: '–' | first | split: ' - ' | first | strip | truncatewords: 3, ''
  endif
  assign env2_pinname = env2_pinname | strip
-%}
{%- assign env2_pinval = '' -%}
{%- if env2_pin_set == '1' -%}
  {%- if env2_meas == '1' and env2_min != '' -%}
    {%- capture env2_pinval -%}<bdi>{{ env2_min }}</bdi> {{ env2_ulab }}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- elsif env2_v1 != '' and env2_v1.size < 19 -%}
    {%- capture env2_pinval -%}{{ env2_v1 | escape }}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- capture env2_pinval -%}{%- render 'elmsnest-v2-price', product: env2_pin -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- liquid
  # The photograph. The four collection.images are the only four in the whole family with no baked
  # text and no cream ground (3.6.4), so the order is: the merchant image, then collection.image, then
  # the image of the collection named in fallback_collection - which is what /collections/all, having
  # no image of its own, is served. A PRODUCT image is deliberately NOT a fallback: the resolver only
  # promises "no baked text", and the one product frame that qualifies on /all is a cream studio
  # ground, which 3.1 and do-not 10 bar as a surface. With no safe photograph the gate falls back to
  # the night ground and the pin is not drawn over nothing (4.1 n-n 4).
  assign env2_img = section.settings.image
  if env2_img == blank
    assign env2_img = collection.image
  endif
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  The guard is the RENDERED url, but image_url on a nil image raises a Liquid error that Shopify
  prints INTO the capture — so an unset picker would come back non-blank and the section would draw a
  broken <img> and skip its own fallback. Measured on /collections/all, which owns no image. The
  object test stops the filter from running at all, and the scrub is the belt for any engine that
  still emits one.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture env2_src -%}{%- if env2_img != blank -%}{{ env2_img | image_url: width: 1800 }}{%- endif -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign env2_src = env2_src | strip -%}
{%- if env2_src contains 'Liquid error' -%}{%- assign env2_src = '' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if env2_src == '' and section.settings.fallback_collection != blank -%}
  {%- assign env2_img = collections[section.settings.fallback_collection].image -%}
  {%- capture env2_src -%}{%- if env2_img != blank -%}{{ env2_img | image_url: width: 1800 }}{%- endif -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign env2_src = env2_src | strip -%}
  {%- if env2_src contains 'Liquid error' -%}{%- assign env2_src = '' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- liquid
  # the guard is the resolved URL, not the object: an image object that resolves to nothing would
  # otherwise print a <picture> with an empty src and a veil over a hole.
  assign env2_hasphoto = false
  if env2_src != ''
    assign env2_hasphoto = true
  endif
  assign env2_focus = env2_map_fd | default: section.settings.image_position_desktop | default: '50% 45%'
  assign env2_focusm = env2_map_fm | default: section.settings.image_position_mobile | default: '50% 50%'
  assign env2_px = env2_map_x | default: section.settings.pin_x | default: 42
  assign env2_py = env2_map_y | default: section.settings.pin_y | default: 28
  assign env2_pxm = env2_map_xm | default: section.settings.pin_x_m | default: 50
  assign env2_pym = env2_map_ym | default: section.settings.pin_y_m | default: 24
  assign env2_stem = section.settings.pin_stem | default: 120
  # The tag hangs from the stem toward the END side by default. Past the middle of the frame that runs
  # it off the edge, so the tag is flipped to hang toward the START side instead - decided here, per
  # viewport, because CSS cannot branch on the value of a custom property.
  assign env2_pinflip = ''
  assign env2_pxn = env2_px | plus: 0
  assign env2_pxmn = env2_pxm | plus: 0
  if env2_pxn > 45
    assign env2_pinflip = ' env2-coll-scene__pinwrap--flip'
  endif
  if env2_pxmn > 45
    assign env2_pinflip = env2_pinflip | append: ' env2-coll-scene__pinwrap--flipm'
  endif
  # and how much room the tag actually has on that side. The photograph is full-bleed, so one percent
  # of the frame is one vw and the room can be written as a length the tag can cap itself with - which
  # is the only way an absolutely positioned tag inside a zero-width pin can be kept off the edge.
  assign env2_room = 100 | minus: env2_pxn
  if env2_pxn > 45
    assign env2_room = env2_pxn
  endif
  assign env2_roomm = 100 | minus: env2_pxmn
  if env2_pxmn > 45
    assign env2_roomm = env2_pxmn
  endif

  assign env2_dp = collection.description | split: '</p>'
  assign env2_p1 = env2_dp[0] | strip_html | strip
  assign env2_p2 = ''
  if env2_dp.size > 1
    assign env2_p2 = env2_dp[1] | strip_html | strip
  endif
  assign env2_ci = section.settings.card_image_index | default: 0 | plus: 0
  if env2_map_ci != ''
    assign env2_ci = env2_map_ci | plus: 0
  endif
  assign env2_cimg = ''
  if env2_ci > 0
    assign env2_cimg = env2_ci
  endif
  # QA-01. The pin is drawn only when every one of its four facts is real (4.1 non-negotiable 4), and
  # the mobile type block has to reserve the tag's band ONLY when it is drawn — so the flag is computed
  # here, once, and printed both as a modifier class and as the unitless per-cent the reserve is built
  # from. --env2-pin-ym carries the % for the dot; --env2-pin-ymn carries the same number with no unit
  # so calc() can turn it into a px band out of --env2-scene-hm, which is a length.
  assign env2_haspin = false
  if env2_pin_set == '1' and env2_hasphoto and env2_pinname != '' and env2_pinval != ''
    assign env2_haspin = true
  endif
-%}
<section id="env2-coll-scene" data-env2-coll-scene class="env2-section env2-coll env2-coll-scene{% if env2_haspin %} env2-coll-scene--pinned{% endif %}" dir="rtl" style="scroll-margin-top:90px;--env2-stars:0;--env2-pin-ymn:{{ env2_pym }};--env2-scene-focus:{{ env2_focus }};--env2-scene-focus-m:{{ env2_focusm }};--env2-scene-hm:{{ section.settings.image_height_mobile | default: 78 }}svh">
  <div class="env2-coll-scene__stage{% unless env2_hasphoto %} env2-coll-scene__stage--noimg{% endunless %}">
    <div class="env2-coll-scene__media">
      {%- if env2_hasphoto -%}
      <picture class="env2-coll-scene__pic">
        <source media="(max-width:900px)" srcset="{{ env2_img | image_url: width: 1000 }}">
        <img src="{{ env2_img | image_url: width: 1800 }}"
             srcset="{{ env2_img | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w, {{ env2_img | image_url: width: 1400 }} 1400w, {{ env2_img | image_url: width: 1800 }} 1800w, {{ env2_img | image_url: width: 2400 }} 2400w"
             sizes="100vw" width="{{ env2_img.width | default: 1800 }}" height="{{ env2_img.height | default: 2250 }}"
             loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"
             alt="{{ env2_img.alt | default: collection.title | escape }}">
      </picture>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span class="env2-coll-scene__wash" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="env2-coll-scene__veil" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {%- if env2_haspin -%}
      <div class="env2-coll-scene__pinwrap{{ env2_pinflip }}" data-lamp
           style="--env2-pin-xd:{{ env2_px }}%;--env2-pin-yd:{{ env2_py }}%;--env2-pin-xm:{{ env2_pxm }}%;--env2-pin-ym:{{ env2_pym }}%;--env2-pin-stem-d:{{ env2_stem }}px;--env2-pin-room-d:calc({{ env2_room }}vw - 18px);--env2-pin-room-m:calc({{ env2_roomm }}vw - 18px)">
        <span class="env2-coll-scene__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="env2-coll-scene__stem" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <a class="env2-coll-scene__pin" href="{{ env2_pin.url }}">
          <span class="env2-coll-scene__tag"><span class="env2-coll-scene__tagtext"><span class="env2-coll-scene__tagname">{{ env2_pinname | escape }}</span> <span class="env2-coll-scene__tagsep" aria-hidden="true">·</span> <span class="env2-coll-scene__tagval">{{ env2_pinval }}</span></span></span>
        </a>
      </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="env2-wrap env2-coll-scene__inner">
      <div class="env2-coll-scene__type">
        <p class="env2-eyebrow env2-coll-scene__eyebrow">{{ env2_eyebrow }}</p>
        <h1 class="env2-h env2-coll-scene__h1">{{ env2_t1 }}{% if env2_t2 != '' %} <span class="env2-glow env2-coll-scene__h1b">{{ env2_t2 }}</span>{% endif %}</h1>
        {%- if env2_deck != '' -%}<p class="env2-lead env2-coll-scene__deck">{{ env2_deck }}</p>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if env2_suits != '' -%}<p class="env2-coll-scene__suits">{{ env2_suits }}</p>{%- endif -%}
        <hr class="env2-hair env2-coll-scene__rule">
        <p class="env2-coll-scene__counts">
          {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign env2_bv = ''
                case block.settings.value
                  when 'products'
                    assign env2_bv = collection.products_count
                  when 'variants'
                    assign env2_bv = env2_nv
                  when 'span'
                    assign env2_bv = env2_span
                  when 'from'
                    if env2_hi > 0
                      assign env2_bv = env2_lo_s
                    endif
                  when 'to'
                    if env2_hi > 0
                      assign env2_bv = env2_hi_s
                    endif
                  when 'catalogue'
                    assign env2_bv = collection.all_products_count
                endcase
              -%}
              {%- if env2_bv != '' -%}
              <span class="env2-coll-scene__count"{{ block.shopify_attributes }}><bdi>{{ env2_bv }}</bdi>{% if block.settings.label != blank %} {{ block.settings.label }}{% endif %}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="env2-coll-scene__count"><bdi>{{ collection.products_count }}</bdi> מנורות</span>
            <span class="env2-coll-scene__count"><bdi>{{ env2_nv }}</bdi> וריאציות</span>
            {%- if env2_span != '' -%}<span class="env2-coll-scene__count"><bdi>{{ env2_span }}</bdi> ₪</span>{%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>
        {%- assign env2_narrow = section.settings.narrow_label | default: '' -%}
        {%- if env2_narrow != '' -%}
        <p class="env2-coll-scene__narrow">
          <a class="env2-coll-scene__narrowlink" href="#env2-coll-ruler">
            <span class="env2-coll-scene__narrowq">{{ env2_narrow }}</span>
            <span class="env2-coll-scene__narrowgo">{{ section.settings.narrow_link_label | default: 'לסרגל המידה' }}<span aria-hidden="true"> ←</span></span>
          </a>
        </p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if env2_pin_set == '1' -%}
      <div class="env2-coll-scene__card">
        {% render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-card', product: env2_pin, variant: 'scene', width: 420, aspect: '1/.72',
                  image_index: env2_cimg, kicker: 'none', action_label: env2_act, heading_level: 2,
                  add_label: section.settings.card_add_label, axis_caption: env2_axisline,
                  unit_price_line: env2_unitline, glyph: 'auto' %}
      </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if env2_p1 != '' or env2_p2 != '' -%}
  <div class="env2-wrap env2-coll-scene__below">
    <div class="env2-coll-scene__desc">
      {%- if section.settings.show_description_p1 and env2_p1 != '' -%}
        <p class="env2-coll-scene__p">{{ env2_p1 }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.show_description_p2 and env2_p2 != '' -%}
        <p class="env2-coll-scene__p env2-coll-scene__p--2">{{ env2_p2 }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    {%- comment -%}
      QA-05 / TYPOGRAPHER-08 — the scene offers ONE door to the ruler. Since LEAD-01 the narrow row
      ships in the fold with the same href; this second link, 141px below it under a different name at
      a different size, was the same destination twice in four tab stops. It now renders only when the
      row is switched off (narrow_label blank), so a merchant who removes the row keeps a route.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.next_label != blank and env2_narrow == '' -%}
    <p class="env2-coll-scene__next"><a class="env2-link" href="{{ section.settings.next_anchor | default: '#env2-coll-ruler' }}">{{ section.settings.next_label }} <span aria-hidden="true">←</span></a></p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</section>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
/* ElmsNest v2 collection — 4.1 the gate. Every selector is .env2-coll-scene__…, nothing here restyles
   a core class, and no section paints a background: the only surface is the scrim card (3.1). */
.env2-coll-scene{padding-block:0;overflow-x:clip}
/* the photograph's mobile height is derived, never consumed raw: --env2-scene-hm is the merchant's own
   setting (image_height_mobile, inline on the section root) and --env2-scene-h is what the mobile block
   actually measures with, so the narrowest viewports can bound the merchant's number in ONE place
   instead of the layout being re-authored around a second constant. Above 360px it is the setting. */
.env2-coll-scene{--env2-scene-h:var(--env2-scene-hm,78svh)}
.env2-coll-scene__stage{position:relative;isolation:isolate}
.env2-coll-scene__media{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:0;overflow:hidden;background:#05070c}
.env2-coll-scene__pic{display:block;position:absolute;inset:0}
.env2-coll-scene__pic img{inline-size:100%;block-size:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:var(--env2-scene-focus,50% 45%);
  display:block;filter:brightness(.6) saturate(.84) contrast(1.02)}
/* the night wash under the veil: the four collection photographs are warm and bright and the h1, the
   eyebrow and the counts line are read straight off them. Without it the gold eyebrow on a lit garland
   is under 3:1 (3.1, 3.2). It is one gradient, it paints no colour of its own, and it stops at the veil. */
.env2-coll-scene__wash{position:absolute;inset:0;pointer-events:none;
  background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(2,3,6,.66) 0%,rgba(2,3,6,.32) 22%,rgba(2,3,6,.26) 44%,rgba(7,11,21,.6) 70%,rgba(15,26,47,.8) 100%)}
/* the two-stop veil over the bottom of the photograph (4.1): the type block and the counts line sit on
   it, and it lands on --env2-sky-2 so the photograph joins the ground with no seam. */
.env2-coll-scene__veil{position:absolute;inset-inline:0;inset-block-end:0;block-size:46%;pointer-events:none;
  background:
    radial-gradient(132% 94% at 100% 100%,rgba(4,7,13,.62) 0%,rgba(4,7,13,0) 62%),
    linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(15,26,47,0) 0%,rgba(15,26,47,.58) 36%,rgba(15,26,47,.84) 66%,#0f1a2f 100%)}
.env2-coll-scene__stage--noimg .env2-coll-scene__media{background:
  radial-gradient(120% 80% at 50% 0%,rgba(31,51,87,.55),rgba(2,3,6,0) 70%),#050a14}

.env2-coll-scene__inner{box-sizing:border-box;position:relative;z-index:2;display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,var(--env2-scene-cardw,420px));
  align-items:end;gap:clamp(28px,4vw,72px);min-block-size:100svh;padding-block:clamp(120px,14vh,168px) clamp(56px,7vh,84px)}
.env2-coll-scene__type{max-inline-size:min(100%,640px)}
/* the eyebrow is a flex row whose box would otherwise span the whole column: hugging its own content
   keeps the 12px gold off the bright half of the photograph (measured 4.36 -> 9+ over decor). */
.env2-coll-scene__eyebrow{inline-size:max-content;max-inline-size:100%;margin-block-end:clamp(16px,2vh,26px);
  text-shadow:0 1px 12px rgba(2,3,6,.9)}
.env2-coll-scene__h1{font-size:clamp(38px,5.8vw,84px);line-height:.98;max-inline-size:22ch;
  text-shadow:0 2px 34px rgba(2,3,6,.75)}
/* TYPOGRAPHER-01 — the two-tone headline is a COLOUR change, not a line break. display:block split
   the h1 into two inline formatting contexts, which forced a break before the last word on every URL
   (wall 208/107, spot 250/627/165 at 1440) and made the .env2-h text-wrap:balance inert. Inline gives
   the balancer back the whole title and lets the colour break fall wherever the line falls. */
.env2-coll-scene__h1b{display:inline}
.env2-coll-scene__deck{margin-block-start:clamp(14px,2vh,22px);max-inline-size:38ch;color:var(--env2-ink-2);
  text-shadow:0 1px 18px rgba(2,3,6,.7)}
.env2-coll-scene__suits{margin:10px 0 0;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;
  max-inline-size:44ch;color:var(--env2-ink-2);text-wrap:pretty;text-shadow:0 1px 18px rgba(2,3,6,.7)}
.env2-coll-scene__rule{margin-block-start:clamp(18px,2.6vh,30px)}
.env2-coll-scene__counts{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:6px 18px;margin:14px 0 0;
  font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--env2-ink-2);
  font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.env2-coll-scene__count{display:inline-flex;align-items:baseline;gap:.35em;white-space:nowrap}
.env2-coll-scene__count+.env2-coll-scene__count::before{content:"·";margin-inline-end:.6em;color:var(--env2-mute)}
.env2-coll-scene__count bdi{color:var(--env2-ink)}
.env2-coll-scene__narrow{margin:12px 0 0;padding-block-start:12px;border-block-start:1px solid var(--env2-hair)}
.env2-coll-scene__narrowlink{position:relative;display:inline-flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:.55em;
  min-height:44px;align-content:center;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-size:15px;line-height:1.4;color:var(--env2-ink-2);text-decoration:none}
.env2-coll-scene__narrowlink::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:-6px -8px}
.env2-coll-scene__narrowq{color:var(--env2-ink)}
.env2-coll-scene__narrowgo{font-size:13.5px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.02em;color:var(--env2-gold);
  border-block-end:1px solid rgba(233,185,110,.42);padding-block-end:2px;transition:color .3s,border-color .3s}
.env2-coll-scene__narrowlink:hover .env2-coll-scene__narrowgo,
.env2-coll-scene__narrowlink:focus-visible .env2-coll-scene__narrowgo{color:var(--env2-glow);border-block-end-color:var(--env2-glow)}

/* the pinned card is elmsnest-v2-pdp-card variant:'scene' — the scrim of 3.1, never hand-rolled here */
.env2-coll-scene__card{justify-self:end;inline-size:100%;max-inline-size:var(--env2-scene-cardw,420px)}
.env2-coll-scene__card .env2-pdp-card{box-sizing:border-box;inline-size:100%}
.env2-coll-scene__card .env2-pdp-card__price .env2-price{--env2-price-size:34px}
.env2-coll-scene__card .env2-pdp-card__title{font-size:clamp(16px,1.3vw,19px)}
/* elmsnest-v2-core sizes .env2-btn content-box, so the ground snippet's 44px floor lands on the
   CONTENT box and the small pill comes out 64px tall on desktop and 72px on a phone. Sized from this
   section's own selector to 3.2's 48px, which is still above the 44px floor. */
.env2-coll-scene__card .env2-pdp-card__action .env2-btn{box-sizing:border-box;min-block-size:48px}

/* the pin (graft C10): a lit dot on the lamp, a hairline stem, a gold tag that names the lamp and
   prints its real value. The DOT never moves - it is on the lamp - but the TAG lands on a fixed band,
   and the stem simply spans whatever is between them. That is what keeps the tag off the h1 and the
   eyebrow on every one of the five photographs and both viewports, which a fixed 120px fall does not:
   measured, the spot and path pins landed on top of the eyebrow at a fixed fall. --env2-pin-stem is
   still the nominal fall; the band is the ceiling it is clamped to. */
.env2-coll-scene__pinwrap{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:3;pointer-events:none;
  --env2-pin-x:var(--env2-pin-xd,42%);--env2-pin-y:var(--env2-pin-yd,28%);
  --env2-pin-stem:var(--env2-pin-stem-d,120px);--env2-pin-band:34%;--env2-pin-room:var(--env2-pin-room-d,340px);
  --env2-pin-top:min(calc(var(--env2-pin-y) + var(--env2-pin-stem)),var(--env2-pin-band))}
.env2-coll-scene__dot{position:absolute;inset-inline-start:var(--env2-pin-x);inset-block-start:var(--env2-pin-y);
  inline-size:10px;block-size:10px;margin-inline-start:-5px;margin-block-start:-5px;
  border-radius:50%;background:var(--env2-glow);opacity:calc(.25 + .75*var(--lit,1));
  box-shadow:0 0 0 calc(6px*var(--lit,1)) rgba(255,211,148,.14),0 0 34px calc(10px*var(--lit,1)) rgba(255,196,110,.5);
  transition:opacity .5s,box-shadow .5s}
.env2-coll-scene__stem{position:absolute;inset-inline-start:var(--env2-pin-x);
  inset-block-start:min(var(--env2-pin-y),var(--env2-pin-top));
  block-size:max(2px,calc(max(var(--env2-pin-y),var(--env2-pin-top)) - min(var(--env2-pin-y),var(--env2-pin-top))));
  inline-size:1px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(255,211,148,.85),rgba(255,211,148,.3));
  transform-origin:top;transform:scaleY(var(--lit,1));transition:transform .45s .15s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)}
.env2-coll-scene__pin{position:absolute;pointer-events:auto;display:block;inline-size:0;
  inset-inline-start:var(--env2-pin-x);inset-block-start:var(--env2-pin-top);text-decoration:none}
/* TYPOGRAPHER-03 — the tag carries a product NAME. 3.2 reserves the 11.5px/.16em tracked style for
   labels and sets 13px as the floor for anything information-bearing; Hebrew is unicase and .16em at
   11.5px dissolves the word shape a Hebrew reader depends on. 13px Heebo 400 at .02em.
   CREATIVE-08 — and the surface is the scrim the page already owns, not a second opaque chip. */
.env2-coll-scene__tag{position:absolute;inset-block-start:0;inset-inline-start:0;box-sizing:border-box;
  display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-block-size:44px;padding-inline:12px;white-space:nowrap;
  inline-size:max-content;max-inline-size:min(var(--env2-pin-room),340px);
  font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-size:13px;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:.02em;color:var(--env2-gold);
  border-radius:0;box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 0 rgba(233,185,110,.55);
  background:rgba(5,8,14,.55);backdrop-filter:blur(8px);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(8px);opacity:calc(.15 + .85*var(--lit,1));transition:opacity .5s .3s,color .3s}
.env2-coll-scene__pinwrap--flip .env2-coll-scene__tag{inset-inline-start:auto;inset-inline-end:0}
.env2-coll-scene__pin:hover .env2-coll-scene__tag,
.env2-coll-scene__pin:focus-visible .env2-coll-scene__tag{color:var(--env2-glow)}
/* QA-04 — the anchor's only child is absolutely positioned out of it, so its border box is 0x0 and
   the focus ring painted an 8px gold square beside the tag. Ring the tag the user is actually on. */
.env2-coll-scene__pin:focus-visible{outline:none}
.env2-coll-scene__pin:focus-visible .env2-coll-scene__tag{outline:2px solid var(--env2-glow);outline-offset:3px}
.env2-coll-scene__tag bdi{letter-spacing:0;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.env2-coll-scene__tagname{unicode-bidi:isolate}
.env2-coll-scene__tagtext{display:inline}
.env2-coll-scene__tagsep{color:var(--env2-mute)}
.env2-coll-scene__tagval{font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0;color:var(--env2-glow);
  font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;unicode-bidi:isolate}

/* below the veil: the collection's own first paragraph, and the route on to the ruler */
.env2-coll-scene__below{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,auto);align-items:start;
  gap:clamp(20px,3vw,56px);padding-block:clamp(34px,5vh,56px) clamp(40px,6vh,72px)}
/* TYPOGRAPHER-02 — 62ch of Heebo sets 76 Hebrew characters to the line (Hebrew glyphs are narrower
   than the ch unit's zero), against 38ch for every other paragraph in the system. 50ch measures 60–62
   real characters and lands inside the 640px h1 column above it, so the two measures now step down
   instead of jumping outward. */
.env2-coll-scene__p{margin:0;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:clamp(15px,1.15vw,17px);
  line-height:1.65;max-inline-size:50ch;color:var(--env2-ink-2);text-wrap:pretty}
.env2-coll-scene__p--2{margin-block-start:10px;color:var(--env2-mute)}
.env2-coll-scene__next{margin:0;justify-self:end}
.env2-coll-scene__card .env2-pdp-card__title a{display:inline-block;padding-block:12px;margin-block:-12px}
.env2-coll-scene__next .env2-link{position:relative}
.env2-coll-scene__next .env2-link::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:-11px -8px}

@media (max-width:900px){
  .env2-coll-scene__media{inset-block-end:auto;block-size:var(--env2-scene-h)}
  .env2-coll-scene__pic img{object-position:var(--env2-scene-focus-m,50% 50%)}
  .env2-coll-scene__veil{block-size:60%}
  .env2-coll-scene__inner{display:block;min-block-size:0;padding-block:0}
  /* the photograph keeps its 78svh; the type block stops --env2-scene-lift above its foot so the card
     rides the last band of the veil and its buy control lands well inside the 844px fold (4.1 n-n 1).
     Measured with the widest card in the catalogue (the wall pair, whose title wraps to three lines
     and whose price is a range): 788px at 390 and 776px at 360. */
  .env2-coll-scene__type{box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;
    max-inline-size:100%;min-block-size:calc(var(--env2-scene-h) - var(--env2-scene-lift,84px));
    padding-block:76px 14px}
  /* ---- QA-01 (blocker) --------------------------------------------------------------------------
     The tag was pinned at a per-cent of the PHOTOGRAPH while the type block's content is bottom-set
     inside (photo - 84px) and rises as the viewport shortens, so below ~740px tall they crossed: at
     390x664 the tag printed across the eyebrow and the h1 on decor, path and spot, and at 320x568 on
     four of five URLs. Reserving a band with a constant would not close it either, because the tag's
     own height is the thing that varies (44px on wall, 78px on spot at 320).

     The two blocks are now coupled by ONE number. --env2-scene-tagtop is the tag's block start, in px,
     resolved from the merchant's pin_y_m per-cent of the photograph and floored at 72px (clear of the
     60px header) so it rises as the photograph shortens; the type block's padding-block-start is that
     same number plus the tag's reserve. contentTop is therefore >= tagTop + tagres BY CONSTRUCTION at
     every viewport height, whatever the tag's per-cent, so the collision cannot come back — the only
     thing a merchant can change is how much room the fold spends on it.
     --env2-scene-tagres is the tag's own box (44px min, up to two 13px lines = 56px) plus 14px clear.
     At 390x844 the ceiling never binds and the padding never exceeds the natural content top, so the
     fold the lead and the creative director measured is byte-identical; the cost is only paid on the
     short viewports where the overlap was.                                                        */
  .env2-coll-scene{--env2-scene-tagres:72px;
    --env2-scene-tagtop:clamp(72px,
      calc(var(--env2-pin-ymn,24) * var(--env2-scene-h) / 100),
      max(72px,calc(var(--env2-scene-h) - 400px)))}
  .env2-coll-scene--pinned .env2-coll-scene__type{
    padding-block-start:max(76px,calc(var(--env2-scene-tagtop) + var(--env2-scene-tagres)))}
  .env2-coll-scene__h1{max-inline-size:16ch}
  .env2-coll-scene__deck{margin-block-start:10px;font-size:16px;max-inline-size:34ch}
  .env2-coll-scene__suits{font-size:14px;margin-block-start:8px}
  .env2-coll-scene__rule{margin-block-start:14px}
  .env2-coll-scene__counts{margin-block-start:10px;font-size:14px;gap:4px 14px}
  .env2-coll-scene__narrow{margin-block-start:8px;padding-block-start:9px}
  .env2-coll-scene__narrowlink{font-size:14.5px;gap:.4em}
  .env2-coll-scene__narrowgo{font-size:13px}
  /* the card rides the foot of the veil so its buy control lands inside the 844px fold (4.1 n-n 1);
     the photograph above it is already the lamp in its place, so the card's own thumbnail is dropped
     rather than shown twice. */
  .env2-coll-scene__card{inline-size:100%;max-inline-size:100%;position:relative;z-index:2;margin-block-start:0}
  .env2-coll-scene__card .env2-pdp-card__media{display:none}
  .env2-coll-scene__card .env2-pdp-card__price .env2-price{--env2-price-size:30px}
  .env2-coll-scene__card .env2-pdp-card{gap:8px}
  .env2-coll-scene__pinwrap{--env2-pin-x:var(--env2-pin-xm,50%);--env2-pin-y:var(--env2-pin-ym,24%);
    --env2-pin-stem:56px;--env2-pin-band:var(--env2-scene-tagtop,24%);--env2-pin-room:var(--env2-pin-room-m,74vw)}
  .env2-coll-scene__pinwrap--flip .env2-coll-scene__tag{inset-inline-start:0;inset-inline-end:auto}
  .env2-coll-scene__pinwrap--flipm .env2-coll-scene__tag{inset-inline-start:auto;inset-inline-end:0}
  /* belt: a long lamp name can never be cut at the frame edge — it wraps inside the tag instead */
  .env2-coll-scene__tag{white-space:normal;max-inline-size:min(var(--env2-pin-room),300px);
    padding-block:9px;line-height:1.45}
  .env2-coll-scene__below{display:block;padding-block:30px 40px}
  .env2-coll-scene__next{margin-block-start:18px}
}
/* ---- QA-02 (regression from the QA-01 fix) -------------------------------------------------------
   Reserving the tag's band above the type block pushed the buy control below a 568px fold on four of
   the five collections, and the first prescription — scale the photograph by .8 at <=360 — was measured
   INERT at 320x568: the buy control sat at the same pixel with the photograph at 443, 416, 399, 354 and
   221px. The reason is --env2-scene-tagtop above. Its ceiling is max(72px, photo - 400px), so once the
   photograph is under 472px the ceiling IS the 72px floor and the tag band is a constant 144px that no
   further shrinking can lower; at 320x568 the photograph is 443px before anything is done to it, so a
   scale there only slides the copy off the picture onto the veil and buys nothing.

   So the photograph is CAPPED, not scaled — 472px is the exact height at which the ceiling reaches the
   floor, i.e. the last pixel that is still load-bearing. min() means the merchant's setting is still the
   number in charge and is never exceeded: at 320x568 (443px) the cap does not bind at all and the
   picture is untouched, at 360x640 it takes 499px to 472px and returns the tag band's 27px to the fold.
   Scoped to <=360 because 78svh is over 472px on a 390 phone too (658px at 390x844, 518px at 390x664),
   where the ceiling is genuinely above the floor and the deeper band is the composition as approved —
   an unconditional cap would rewrite the 390x844 fold the lead and the creative director signed off.

   320x568 is not closed by this and is not meant to be: the stack there is a 144px tag band + 310px of
   copy + 14px padding before the card, the photograph contributes nothing to it, and the levers that
   would close it all cost more than the 43px they buy. Ruled OPEN and accepted at <=320; 360x640 is the
   line that must stay inside the fold.                                                             */
@media (max-width:360px){
  .env2-coll-scene{--env2-scene-h:min(var(--env2-scene-hm,78svh),472px)}
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  .env2-coll-scene__dot,.env2-coll-scene__stem,.env2-coll-scene__tag{transition:none}
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% javascript %}
/* elmsnest-v2-coll-scene — 4.1. The gate is server-rendered and buyable with scripting off; the only
   thing this file does is register the pin as a lamp so the dot lights and the stem draws on arrival
   (3.3), and light it outright when window.env2 is not there. Nothing else in screen 1 moves. */
(function () {
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-env2-coll-scene]').forEach(function (el) {
    window.env2 ? env2.observe(el) : el.querySelectorAll('[data-lamp]').forEach(function (l) { l.classList.add('lit'); });
  });
})();
{% endjavascript %}

